    "result_text": "The full suite is green (`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class with `@Test` methods; it's the black-box acceptance harness the feature is graded against).\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the soft-match \"possible duplicate\" feature. A new owner that isn't a hard duplicate but shares an existing owner's `lastName` + `postcode` with a **different telephone** is still created, and its response now carries `possibleDuplicate: true` with `possibleDuplicateOf` set to the matching owner's id (earliest match when several exist); otherwise `possibleDuplicate: false`.\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added two read-only properties to the `Owner` schema: `possibleDuplicate` (boolean) and `possibleDuplicateOf` (int32). The `OwnerDto` is code-generated from this, and MapStruct auto-maps them by name (same pattern as `bulkSignupWarning`).\n\n2. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 Added two `@Transient` (never persisted, response-time derived) fields `possibleDuplicate`/`possibleDuplicateOf` with getters/setters.\n\n3. **`AssignOwnerPossibleDuplicate.java`** (new function step) \u2014 Compares the owner against all others (excluding itself): `lastName` case-insensitively, `postcode` exactly (requires a non-blank postcode), and telephone in canonical E.164 form must **differ**. Picks the lowest-id match, mirroring the existing `AssignOwnerNamesakeCount`/`AssignOwnerHouseholdSize` steps.\n\n4. **Pipeline wiring** \u2014 Added the step after `householdSize` on both `owners.POST.yml` (create) and `owners/{ownerId}.GET.yml` (read), so the flag is recomputed identically whether returned from the create response or a later GET \u2014 matching how the test reads it back via `GET`.\n\nThe existing hard-duplicate 409 path (`EnsureUniqueOwnerIdentity`) is untouched; this is purely the additive soft-match warning.",
